\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God of pity, God of grace,
\par When we humbly seek Thy face,
\par Bend from heaven, Thy dwelling
\par place;
\par Hear, forgive and save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. When we in Thy temple meet,
\par Spread our wants before Thy  feet,
\par Pleading at Thy mercy- seat,
\par Look from heaven and save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. When Th love our hearts shall fill,
\par And we long to do Thy will,
\par Turning to Thy holy hill,
\par Lord, accept and save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Should we wander from Thy fold,
\par And our love to Thee grow cold,
\par With a pitying eye behold,
\par Lord, forgive and save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Should the hand of sorrow press,
\par Earthly care and want distress
\par May our souls Thy peace possess;
\par Jesus, hear and save.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. And whate'er our cry may be,
\par When we lift our hearts to Thee,
\par From our burden set us free,
\par Hear, forgive and save.
\par                          Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

